  "correct": "3",
  "solution": "**Given:**\n\nSum = Rs. 58000\n\nRate for S.I = 8%\n\nRate for C.I = 10%\n\nTime = 2 years\n\n**Concept used:**\n\nS.I = (P × T × R)/100\n\nC.I = P[(1 + R/100)T - 1]\n\nHere,\n\nP = sum\n\nR = rate\n\nT = time\n\n**Calculation:**\n\nS.I = (58000 × 8 × 2)/100\n\n⇒ 580 × 16\n\n⇒ 9280\n\nAgain,\n\nC.I = 58000[(1 + 10/100)² - 1]\n\n⇒ 58000[(1 + 1/10)² - 1]\n\n⇒ 58000[(11/10)² - 1]\n\n⇒ 58000[(121/100) - 1]\n\n⇒ 58000[(121 - 100)/100]\n\n⇒ 58000 × (21/100)\n\n⇒ 12180\n\nSo, difference = 12180 - 9280\n\n⇒ Rs. 2900\n\n**∴ He earned 2900 (in ₹) in the transaction at the end of 2 years.**",
